notes               = "Untitled in source. The prayer in guillemets (lines 9-15) is spoken by زنی, a woman, not by the poet. The poem's shape is a water cycle — rain falls on the cypress, runs to the river, the river to the sea, the sea back up as cloud — stated twice, the second time widened from one cypress to all the cypresses of the world. 7 Azar = 28 November 2002. Imported as a draft with machine / lantern layers; ===translation=== left for Ben."
